R(id="r3",time="19:00",theme="dark",tag="MONEY MATH",area="BRAMPTON",fmt="money-math (everyday, $10K prepayment on a $500K mortgage)",aud="buyer",series="money-math",math="everyday",
 hook="$10K bonus. Interest *saved?",kick="$10K VS INTEREST",hprop="piggy",hsay="Brampton: could ten thousand dollars save interest?",
 calc=[("Monthly mortgage on $500,000, 25 years","$2,723","$500,000 mortgage, 4.34% example rate, 25 years","$2,723 a month","calculator","First, a five hundred thousand dollar mortgage over twenty-five years is about two thousand, seven hundred twenty-three dollars a month."),
       ("Owing after one year, then a $10K prepayment","$478,607","$488,607 after 12 payments - $10,000","$478,607 owing","piggy","Next, after one year you would owe about four hundred eighty-eight thousand, six hundred seven, and a ten thousand dollar prepayment brings that to four hundred seventy-eight thousand, six hundred seven."),
       ("Interest over the whole mortgage","$299,352","vs $316,920 with no prepayment, same monthly mortgage","Interest: $316,920 down to $299,352","chart","Now the twist. Then, keeping the same monthly mortgage, your total interest drops from three hundred sixteen thousand, nine hundred twenty dollars to two hundred ninety-nine thousand, three hundred fifty-two.")],
 total=("Interest saved by the $10K prepayment","$17,568","about 10 months sooner (290 payments instead of 300)","Example only: $500,000 mortgage, 25 years, 4.34% fixed (lowest advertised 5-year fixed, insured, Ratehub.ca, Nov 26, 2026), compounded semi-annually, same rate and monthly mortgage throughout; $10,000 prepaid after payment 12. Prepayment privileges and penalties vary by lender. Not mortgage, tax or legal advice.","Finally, that ten thousand dollars could save about seventeen thousand, five hundred sixty-eight dollars in interest, and about ten months of payments."),
 cta="Like, comment and *share with your co-buyer",csay="Like, comment and share this with your co-buyer. "+CTAW,
 fine="Example only. Not mortgage, tax or legal advice.",
 cap="$10K bonus. Interest saved?\n\nExample only: a $500,000 mortgage in Brampton, 25-year amortization, 4.34% fixed (interest compounded semi-annually, same rate for the whole amortization).\n1) Monthly mortgage: $2,723.07.\n2) After 12 payments the balance is about $488,607. A $10,000 prepayment brings it to $478,607.\n3) Keeping the same monthly mortgage, total interest drops from $316,920 to $299,352, which is $17,568 less, and the mortgage is paid off about 10 months sooner (290 payments instead of 300).\nPrepayment privileges, limits and penalties differ by lender and mortgage, so check yours first. 4.34% is an example from the lowest advertised 5-year fixed rates (insured); uninsured rates can differ, and rates change at renewal. Lenders also apply the stress test and debt ratios.\n\nPlanning a move in Brampton? "+INFO+"\n\nExample only. Not mortgage, tax or legal advice.\nSource: Ratehub.ca, best 5-year fixed mortgage rates (lowest insured 4.34%, as of Nov 26, 2026), checked Nov 27, 2026. Calculations by Krishna Rander's team.",
 tags="#bramptonrealestate #peelregion #mortgagetips #keyswithkrishna",
 pattern="6 tease + reveal",trigger="curiosity about what a bonus could do, surprise at the lifetime saving",share="the co-buyer you're planning with"),
